messages:
maria: Noticed a docs gap: the v1->v2 migration guide shows HTTP status checks in examples but runtime will now send structured error objects (e.g. {code: 'RATE_LIMIT', message: '...'}). We need an appendix mapping the old codes to v2 codes and short tolerant snippets.
kevin: Good catch. We didn't centralize that mapping anywhere. Can we make a tiny canonical table and recommend which fields to use for alerting?
nina: I can draft the PR. Proposal: one mapping table + two lightweight snippets (python + typescript) demonstrating detection of v2 structured error, with fallback to v1 status codes for one release window. Also add a short note on retry semantics.
sam: I'll paste example snippets — keep them minimal so readers can copy/paste into apps. Also suggest we update snippets under docs/snippets/*/error-handling and add CI smoke-tests to run them.
maria: Please add a migration blurb on observability: encourage emitting error.code as a log field and migrating alerts from http_status to error.code. That will make SLA tracking easier. :chart_with_upwards_trend:
sam: Example snippets (feel free to edit):
```python
# tolerant error handling (python)
try:
    resp = client.generate(prompt)
except Exception as e:
    # structured v2 error may be on e.meta or e.body depending on SDK
    payload = getattr(e, 'meta', None) or getattr(e, 'body', None) or {}
    code = payload.get('code') or getattr(e, 'status_code', None)
    if code == 'RATE_LIMIT' or code == 429:
        await backoff_and_retry()
    elif code == 'INVALID_REQUEST' or code == 400:
        raise ClientError('invalid request')
    else:
        raise
```
```ts
// tolerant error handling (ts)
try {
  await client.responses.create({ input: prompt });
} catch (err) {
  const v2Code = err?.response?.data?.code;
  const v1Status = err?.status || err?.response?.status;
  const unified = v2Code ?? v1Status;
  if (unified === 'RATE_LIMIT' || unified === 429) {
    await backoffAndRetry();
  } else if (unified === 'INVALID_REQUEST' || unified === 400) {
    throw new Error('invalid request');
  } else {
    throw err;
  }
}
```
kevin: Solid. Let's include a tiny mapping table row in the PR description: - v1 429 -> v2 'RATE_LIMIT' (retryable) - v1 502/503 -> v2 'TRANSIENT_SERVER_ERROR' (retryable w/ jitter) - v1 400 -> v2 'INVALID_REQUEST' (do not retry)
nina: I'll put that in. Also adding a note: recommend teams prefer error.code for future-proof checks and keep status-code fallback for one release cycle.
